{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.C1InfDegreeLaw","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1InfDegreeLaw","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.ComputeDegree","lean:module:QOU.Mass.C1FormalSolutionGrowth","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QBorelKernelLevel"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ramified_qBorel_budget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ramified_qBorel_budget","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L150-L160","doc":"**S1 budget, exactly.** At the ramified index `N = 2m`, the C1 coefficient\nexponent exceeds the level-2 q-Borel kernel exponent by exactly `m`:\n`m² = m(m−1) + m`. Linear leftover ⇒ the ramified transform converges, whereas\nno unramified level absorbs the quadratic growth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_natDegree_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_natDegree_step","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L128-L133","doc":"The per-step increment, transported to the genuine degree: appending the\nfactor `f_n` raises the polynomial degree by exactly `2n+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_natDegree_eq_c1FormalDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_natDegree_eq_c1FormalDeg","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L121-L126","doc":"**Bridge.** The genuine polynomial degree of `cₙ` is the combinatorial\n`c1FormalDeg n`. This is what connects `QOU.Mass.C1FormalSolutionGrowth.c1FormalDeg` to the object it\nis named for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L96-L103","doc":"**The degree law.** `natDegree cₙ = n²`, for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L91-L94","doc":"`cₙ` is never the zero polynomial — a product of nonzero factors in the\ndomain `ℤ[X]`. This is what licenses additivity of `natDegree` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cFactor_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cFactor_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L76-L89","doc":"Each factor has degree exactly `2m + 1`, including the degenerate `m = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cFactor_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cFactor_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L68-L74","doc":"The factor is never the zero polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cFactor_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cFactor_zero","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L63-L66","doc":"`f₀ = 2X − 1` — the degenerate case where the two `(X−1)` terms collide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cFactor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cFactor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L57-L61","doc":"Expanded normal form of the factor: `f_m = X^{2m+1} − X^{2m} + X^{m+1} − Xᵐ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_succ","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L53-L55","doc":"The recurrence, as stated in the audit: `c_{m+1} = c_m · f_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cCoeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L50-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cCoeff","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L46-L48","doc":"The `∞`-side coefficient `cₙ = ∏_{m<n} f_m`, with `c₀ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cFactor","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1InfDegreeLaw.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The recurrence factor `f_m = 1 + (X−1)Xᵐ + (X−1)X^{2m}` over `ℤ[X]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}